cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
type: preprint
title: "Fully Dynamic Longest Palindromic Substring via Mergeable Palindrome Summaries"
authors:
  - family-names: "Liu"
    given-names: "Chengde"
date-released: "2026-11-21"
license: "CC-BY-4.0"
abstract: >-
  We study the longest palindromic substring problem for a string undergoing
  point updates, insertions, deletions, range reversals, range cyclic shifts,
  and interval LPS queries. An implicit Treap stores per-node palindrome
  summaries (LP, PSuf, PPref as arithmetic progressions, and forward/reverse
  hashes). The complexity is stated in three variants: O(log^4 n) with
  Treap-hash LCE for all operations; O(log^3 n) with GKK dynamic LCE for
  point updates, insertions, deletions and interval queries; and O(log^3 n)
  for the full operation set conditional on an LCE oracle supporting range
  rearrangements. The paper also proves a Theta(log n) lower bound on the
  number of progressions, analyzes batch-LCE and lazy-summary barriers
  within the framework, reports exhaustive/randomized verification and two
  implementations, and treats distinct-palindrome counting as open.
keywords:
  - dynamic strings
  - longest palindromic substring
  - Treap
  - arithmetic progressions
  - LCE
  - data structures
